## Git [pattern]

> Pick the posture that matches how you work; delete the others.

<!-- example: hand git to the human
User runs all git themselves — never invoke git, never add co-author/attribution tags. Write commit messages only when asked.
-->
<!-- example: gated commits
Committing requires human validation unless told otherwise. Follow Conventional Commits. Never add AI attribution or co-author tags.
-->
<!-- example: gated commits + explicit bypass flag
Committing requires human validation unless told otherwise. An explicit `--yes`/`-y` flag (`/<commit-skill> --yes <repo>`) IS that authorization → commit directly. Follow Conventional Commits.
-->

## Paths [pattern]

Aliases, control/data split, locations → `.claude/rules/paths.md`, always loaded. Resolve against its tables; never guess a path.

<!-- Useful once you juggle several repos: "control" = where the instructions live, "data" = the separate repo the work lands in. Template: examples/.claude/rules/paths.md.example. -->

## Temp files [core]

- Temp files: `<scratch-dir>/{task}/` (e.g. `.tmp/{task}/`), NEVER the system `/tmp`. Clean up after.
- `**/.in/`: bootstrap context dropped in by the user (read-only). [pattern]

## Where things go — load tiers [pattern]

> The lever that keeps this file small. Route each piece of content by *when* it is needed:
>
> | Content | Where | Load cost |
> |---|---|---|
> | Triggers + standing biases, needed every turn | `CLAUDE.md` | every session, sub-agents too, survives `/compact` |
> | Small lookup table needed most sessions (alias map) | `.claude/rules/*.md` **without** frontmatter | every session, same as `CLAUDE.md` |
> | Language/domain rules | `.claude/rules/*.md` **with** `paths:` frontmatter (e.g. `"**/*.py"`) | when Claude reads a matching file |
> | Bulky, rarely needed reference (clause menu, procedure) | `.claude/refs/*.md` + a one-line pointer here | only when the pointer fires |
> | Personal cross-session facts | auto-memory | managed by the harness |
>
> Gotchas:
> - A `rules/` file without `paths:` is **not** on-demand — it loads at launch. Only `refs/` (any folder outside `rules/`) behind a pointer is truly lazy.
> - `@path` imports load eagerly at launch — they organize, they don't save context.
> - `outputStyle` applies to the main conversation only; `CLAUDE.md` reaches sub-agents (except built-in Explore/Plan). Rules sub-agents must follow go here.
> - Only the root `CLAUDE.md` is re-injected after `/compact`; path-scoped rules and nested `CLAUDE.md` reload only when a matching file is read again.
> - Personal, uncommitted variant: `CLAUDE.local.md` (gitignored); machine-wide: `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` and `~/.claude/rules/`.
